  "term": "factor analysis",
  "definition": "Factor analysis is a research method used to examine the internal structure of a measure by identifying underlying dimensions within a set of items. In this packet, exploratory and confirmatory factor analysis were used to develop and validate a scale and to show that it included four dimensions.",
